$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Step 1: To a flask containing tert-butyl
((3S,4S)-3-((6-chloro-5-cyanopyrazin-2-yl)amino)-1,1-dioxidotetrahydro-2H-thiopyran-4-yl)carbamate
(10.5 g, 26.1 mmol),
2-(4,4,5,5-tetramethyl-1,3,2-dioxaborolan-2-yl)-1H-indole (7.62 g, 31.4
mmol), and [1,1′-bis(diphenylphosphino)ferrocene]dichloropalladium (II),
complex with dichloromethane (1.07 g, 1.31 mmol) was added dioxane (75
mL) and sodium carbonate (2 M aqueous, 26.1 mL, 52.3 mmol). The mixture
was degassed by sparging with argon (5 min) and heated to 90°C for 1.5 h.
The mixture was allowed to cool to rt, then diluted with dichloromethane
and water. The layers were separated, and the aqueous portion was
extracted with dichloromethane. The combined organic extracts were dried
over magnesium sulfate, filtered, and concentrated in vacuo to afford a
residue, which was adsorbed onto silica gel and purified by normal phase
silica gel column chromatography (EtOAc:Hexanes). The material was then
slurried in EtOAc, and hexanes were added while cooling the mixture to
0°C. The resultant solids were filtered and washed with hexanes.
tert-butyl
((3S,4S)-3-((5-cyano-6-(1H-indol-2-yl)pyrazin-2-yl)amino)-1,1-dioxidotetrahydro-2H-thiopyran-4-yl)carbamate
(10.3 g, 82%) as a brown solid. MS ESI calc’d. for C23H27N6O4S [M + H]+
483, found 483.
